00:01:15.160 --> 00:01:17.260
All these swimming and cricket.

00:01:17.260 --> 00:01:18.893
- It wasn't fancy, I promise you that.

00:01:18.893 --> 00:01:19.840
It's just I went to a boy school

00:01:19.840 --> 00:01:21.900
and the school just had everything.

00:01:21.900 --> 00:01:23.874
- It was an all boys school
- All boys school, yeah.

00:01:23.874 --> 00:01:25.993
- Did you like that?
- Mm.

00:01:25.993 --> 00:01:26.940
(host laughs)

00:01:26.940 --> 00:01:29.290
- I would not have liked
an all girls school.

00:01:29.290 --> 00:01:30.900
- I moved from one area to another area.

00:01:30.900 --> 00:01:32.700
So I started in a mixed school, right?

00:01:32.700 --> 00:01:34.140
I was about 13 years old.

00:01:34.140 --> 00:01:36.120
My mom said, "We're moving
to this other area."

00:01:36.120 --> 00:01:36.953
Okay, great.

00:01:36.953 --> 00:01:37.786
Go into a new school.

00:01:37.786 --> 00:01:38.619
Exciting.

00:01:38.619 --> 00:01:39.452
It's called Trinity.

00:01:39.452 --> 00:01:41.630
I was like, "Great. Going to Trinity."

00:01:41.630 --> 00:01:42.830
The first day before school,

00:01:42.830 --> 00:01:45.047
you put your clothes on the bed.

00:01:45.047 --> 00:01:46.160
"This is what I'm gonna wear tomorrow,

00:01:46.160 --> 00:01:47.410
I'm gonna look so cool."

00:01:47.410 --> 00:01:51.260
Did that, get to the school
and it's lunchtime, okay?

00:01:51.260 --> 00:01:53.980
And the teacher's like, "Welcome
Idris. This is the school."

00:01:53.980 --> 00:01:56.547
And I'm looking over and I said to him,

00:01:56.547 --> 00:01:58.647
"Do the girls eat somewhere else?"

00:01:58.647 --> 00:02:00.000
(audience laughing)

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:00.847
- That's how you found out?

00:02:00.847 --> 00:02:03.564
