00:02:03.564 --> 00:02:04.694
(Idris growls)

00:02:04.694 --> 00:02:06.027
- [Host] Oh my gosh.

00:02:06.027 --> 00:02:07.440
- It was a shock.

00:02:07.440 --> 00:02:08.430
- That's sad.

00:02:08.430 --> 00:02:12.160
- So then (chuckles) I ended
up becoming very competitive.

00:02:12.160 --> 00:02:13.200
- Okay, that's cool.

00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:14.740
All the sports came into play there.

00:02:14.740 --> 00:02:16.404
I'm really glad you didn't do sports

00:02:16.404 --> 00:02:17.760
and you were acting.

00:02:17.760 --> 00:02:19.594
(audience applauding)

00:02:19.594 --> 00:02:21.953
So you had all the guy
friends, no girlfriends,

00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:25.720
but who was your best friend growing up?

00:02:25.720 --> 00:02:27.650
- My best friend was
actually my arch-enemy.

00:02:27.650 --> 00:02:28.940
This kid called Boogie.

00:02:28.940 --> 00:02:30.490
- Your arch-enemy?

00:02:30.490 --> 00:02:32.281
- The first day I got there--

00:02:32.281 --> 00:02:33.379
- I would love to go to therapy with you.

00:02:33.379 --> 00:02:34.930
(everyone laughs)

00:02:34.930 --> 00:02:36.201
- You would learn a lot, honestly.

00:02:36.201 --> 00:02:37.034
(host laughs)

00:02:37.034 --> 00:02:38.590
But the first day I got
there, I was a new kid.

00:02:38.590 --> 00:02:40.956
I got picked on by this one kid.

00:02:40.956 --> 00:02:43.149
He wasn't a big kid,
he just had a mouth.

00:02:43.149 --> 00:02:44.190
It was like motor mouth.

00:02:44.190 --> 00:02:45.180
And he really got at me.

00:02:45.180 --> 00:02:46.860
So we got into a fight,

00:02:46.860 --> 00:02:48.910
ended up outside the headmaster's room,

00:02:48.910 --> 00:02:50.427
headmaster slammed open the door,

00:02:50.427 --> 00:02:52.540
"You're the new kid and Richard,

00:02:52.540 --> 00:02:53.530
you should know better.

00:02:53.530 --> 00:02:54.530
What happened?"

00:02:54.530 --> 00:02:57.010
And we both looked at each other,

00:02:57.010 --> 00:02:58.330
said, "Nothing, sir."

00:02:58.330 --> 00:03:00.277
And we didn't snitch on
each other and that was it.

00:03:00.277 --> 00:03:02.920
And then we just became
best friends since.

00:03:02.920 --> 00:03:04.679
- That's a great story.
(audience applauding)

00:03:04.679 --> 00:03:07.810
- Its a true story.
(audience applauding)

00:03:07.810 --> 00:03:09.100
- He was the best man at my wedding.

00:03:09.100 --> 00:03:10.473
He's still my guy.

00:03:10.473 --> 00:03:11.530
- Oh my gosh.

00:03:11.530 --> 00:03:12.363
That's amazing.

00:03:12.363 --> 00:03:14.110
Well, speaking of fighting,

00:03:14.110 --> 00:03:17.376
Deon Cole had this to say
about working with you.

00:03:17.376 --> 00:03:18.350
(host chuckles)

00:03:18.350 --> 00:03:19.410
- Deon.
(air whooshing)

00:03:19.410 --> 00:03:21.020
- Let me tell you about Idris' ass.

00:03:21.020 --> 00:03:22.840
Check this out.
(audience laughing)

00:03:22.840 --> 00:03:27.840
We practiced for two weeks
straight on this scene, right?

00:03:28.630 --> 00:03:32.180
Of how to fight in the fight, right?

00:03:32.180 --> 00:03:33.193
Two weeks.

00:03:34.631 --> 00:03:35.750
We know it's so much so,

00:03:35.750 --> 00:03:37.250
we're like, "We ain't coming."

00:03:38.780 --> 00:03:41.260
We get first day on the set, we get there.

00:03:41.260 --> 00:03:43.220
all of a sudden they go, "Action,"

00:03:43.220 --> 00:03:45.567
bam, hits me in the head.

00:03:45.567 --> 00:03:47.590
(audience applauding)

00:03:47.590 --> 00:03:50.203
- So what was your memory of that?

00:03:51.130 --> 00:03:53.350
- Maybe you should have
gone to the rehearsals more.

00:03:53.350 --> 00:03:55.530
- So Deon Cole is a comedian, right?

00:03:55.530 --> 00:03:57.770
But he's such a good actor, right?

00:03:57.770 --> 00:03:59.890
And I was like, "This guy's really good."

00:03:59.890 --> 00:04:03.223
So boom, I hit him, but
I didn't mean to hit him.

00:04:05.034 --> 00:04:07.320
I was so embroiled in his character

00:04:07.320 --> 00:04:10.630
that I was like, "Wow, you're
really upsetting me, boom."

00:04:10.630 --> 00:04:11.990
(audience laughing)

00:04:11.990 --> 00:04:15.280
It was a slip, but it did hit
him (pops) right on his head.

00:04:15.280 --> 00:04:17.423
- I'm just saying you're not a small dude.

00:04:18.580 --> 00:04:20.740
When you're hitting someone
you're coming in hot.

00:04:20.740 --> 00:04:21.573
- Little Deon.

00:04:22.680 --> 00:04:23.513
- It was hilarious.

00:04:23.513 --> 00:04:26.114
He was like, "He hit me in my face."

00:04:26.114 --> 00:04:26.947
(Idris laughing)

00:04:26.947 --> 00:04:28.053
(everyone laughs)

00:04:28.053 --> 00:04:29.450
I was like, "Wait don't
y'all do fake moves?"

00:04:29.450 --> 00:04:30.682
He goes, "Yeah, we do."

00:04:30.682 --> 00:04:31.515
- We do.

00:04:31.515 --> 00:04:32.348
We're meant to.

00:04:33.276 --> 00:04:35.428
And he's node just was like, (roaring).

00:04:35.428 --> 00:04:36.300
I was like, (soothing).

00:04:36.300 --> 00:04:38.140
- Kind of a cool wound though.

00:04:38.140 --> 00:04:40.520
Idris Elba hit me in fight.

00:04:40.520 --> 00:04:41.839
I'd be like, "You should see him."

00:04:41.839 --> 00:04:42.878
(Idris laughing)

00:04:42.878 --> 00:04:46.060
So the new movie is called
"Sonic the Hedgehog 2."

00:04:46.060 --> 00:04:47.670
So tell everybody what it's about

00:04:47.670 --> 00:04:49.870
because I didn't really know
these characters growing up.

00:04:49.870 --> 00:04:52.240
I think other people our age might know.

00:04:52.240 --> 00:04:54.050
- Sonic the Hedgehog 2,

00:04:54.050 --> 00:04:57.350
obviously we know he was part
of the game and is very famous

00:04:57.350 --> 00:05:01.100
and Knuckles is one of
his enemies in the game

00:05:01.100 --> 00:05:03.770
or at least ally enemies, whatever.

00:05:03.770 --> 00:05:07.020
And in the film, it's a really great story

00:05:07.020 --> 00:05:08.400
because I don't wanna
spoil it for you guys

00:05:08.400 --> 00:05:09.233
who haven't seen it,

00:05:09.233 --> 00:05:12.370
but when you meet Knuckles,
he is all business.

00:05:12.370 --> 00:05:14.380
He's not here to play, make friends.

00:05:14.380 --> 00:05:16.680
And you're thinking, "Oh,
son's gonna have a hard time."

00:05:16.680 --> 00:05:18.770
But by the end of the movie,
something else happens.

00:05:18.770 --> 00:05:21.420
I don't wanna spoil it for
you, but it's a great arc.

00:05:22.792 --> 00:05:26.233
And Knuckles is this
little guy with big hands.

00:05:27.686 --> 00:05:30.559
- Huge hands.
(Idris laughs)

00:05:30.559 --> 00:05:31.476
I know too.

00:05:32.510 --> 00:05:33.343
That's my favorite part.

00:05:33.343 --> 00:05:35.241
when Sonic comes at him, he is like, "No."

00:05:35.241 --> 00:05:36.074
(chuckles)

00:05:36.074 --> 00:05:36.907
He just holds out his hand.

00:05:36.907 --> 00:05:37.740
It's amazing.
- It's just like that.

00:05:37.740 --> 00:05:39.980
- It's like the big
dude, little dude moment.

00:05:39.980 --> 00:05:42.200
I love the movie and I
love just having kids...

00:05:42.200 --> 00:05:43.991
I have a five and seven year old.

00:05:43.991 --> 00:05:44.824
- I have a seven year old.

00:05:44.824 --> 00:05:46.310
- Oh yeah?
- Yeah.

00:05:46.310 --> 00:05:47.983
- It's such a fun age.

00:05:49.610 --> 00:05:50.970
It's cool when you're watching a movie

00:05:50.970 --> 00:05:52.760
and they learn something from it too,

00:05:52.760 --> 00:05:53.900
especially relationships.

00:05:53.900 --> 00:05:56.230
That's what I love about
Knuckle's kinda journey on it.

00:05:56.230 --> 00:05:59.590
And with Sonic and with
Jim Carrey's character,

00:05:59.590 --> 00:06:02.830
it's interesting how the arch
and how that story helps kids.

00:06:02.830 --> 00:06:04.630
It's a fun thing to watch with your kids,

00:06:04.630 --> 00:06:06.432
but it's also a really good message.

00:06:06.432 --> 00:06:07.265
- That's so true.

00:06:07.265 --> 00:06:08.860
'Cause there's a point
where Sonic and Knuckles

00:06:08.860 --> 00:06:11.870
realize that they're more
alike than they are enemies,

00:06:11.870 --> 00:06:13.210
and that moment's quite rich.

00:06:13.210 --> 00:06:14.450
- This is kinda like you and your friend.

00:06:14.450 --> 00:06:15.901
- Yes.

00:06:15.901 --> 00:06:17.288
(audience applauding)

00:06:17.288 --> 00:06:18.121
- Look at that, it's very much.

00:06:18.121 --> 00:06:21.143
- Did you get a third of this writing?

00:06:22.083 --> 00:06:24.070
They just ripped your story.

00:06:24.070 --> 00:06:25.758
So your son, you said is seven?

00:06:25.758 --> 00:06:26.591
- He's seven.

00:06:26.591 --> 00:06:28.547
He saw the movie and I asked him, I said,

00:06:28.547 --> 00:06:29.590
"What was your favorite part?"

00:06:29.590 --> 00:06:34.200
And he went, "All of it."
(laughs)

00:06:34.200 --> 00:06:36.787
- My God, that's like me asking
my kid, "How was your day?"

00:06:36.787 --> 00:06:37.650
"It was fine."

00:06:37.650 --> 00:06:39.507
Everyday I'm like, "Anything happen?"

00:06:39.507 --> 00:06:40.930
"Nope, just fine."

00:06:40.930 --> 00:06:42.885
I'm like, "Cool, we're
not gonna expand upon?"

00:06:42.885 --> 00:06:43.718
"No, cool."

00:06:43.718 --> 00:06:44.551
"Okay, cool."

00:06:44.551 --> 00:06:46.730
So wait, you also have a
podcast with your wife, Sabrina.

00:06:46.730 --> 00:06:47.680
I think this is so cool.

00:06:47.680 --> 00:06:48.960
It's called "Coupledom."

00:06:48.960 --> 00:06:52.700
So does this help your
relationship or does is it taxing?

00:06:52.700 --> 00:06:54.790
- No, we learn a lot.

00:06:54.790 --> 00:06:58.350
The "Coupledom," isn't really
just about romantic couples,

00:06:58.350 --> 00:06:59.570
it's about partnerships.

00:06:59.570 --> 00:07:01.410
So we have all these great partnerships.

00:07:01.410 --> 00:07:03.060
We spoke to Ben and Jerry, right?

00:07:03.060 --> 00:07:03.893
Ben and Jerry.

00:07:03.893 --> 00:07:05.550
We're a great partnership,
done it for years.

00:07:05.550 --> 00:07:08.740
And we learn from their stories.

00:07:08.740 --> 00:07:11.130
It helps us understand what we have to do

00:07:11.130 --> 00:07:13.870
and things that we haven't
thought about, shortcomings.

00:07:13.870 --> 00:07:15.930
One of the keys is just communication

00:07:15.930 --> 00:07:18.820
and just being honest
and not being too fragile

00:07:18.820 --> 00:07:20.360
when you hear something you don't like,

00:07:20.360 --> 00:07:23.683
just being able to sort
of absorb that, move on.

00:07:24.550 --> 00:07:26.330
But I learned a lot from the podcast.

00:07:26.330 --> 00:07:27.840
I'm not gonna lie, really good stuff.

00:07:27.840 --> 00:07:28.673
- I love that.

00:07:28.673 --> 00:07:29.830
I love that y'all do that together.

00:07:29.830 --> 00:07:31.920
